FerrionOS change to upstream userutils (MIT license, kept), made against upstream commit 641a5aa81574db79d883151bc3438d3e59f90b88 after the existing recipe patches.

One password: login and the new unlock-session command (for the graphical login) start the first session of the account whose key slot opened the volume at startup without a password, once per boot, reading the slot from /scheme/sys/env and the account from the root-only /etc/unlock-slots, never after a recovery-key unlock. passwd changes that account's disk slot through redoxfs-key change in the sudo daemon, in the same operation, and fails when the slot cannot be changed; a password set by root without the old one says the disk keeps the old one.

